From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:00:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 261/289] [ae-patch] Treat a vanished process as dead in the
 process group timeout test

The test probed the grandchild with os.kill and then read /proc/<pid>/stat. If the zombie was reaped between the two calls the read raised FileNotFoundError and failed CI on a correct run. A missing /proc entry now counts as dead, same as a zombie.
---
 .../claude_native/forwarder/test_ae_prompt_suggest.py  | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/harnesses/claude_native/forwarder/test_ae_prompt_suggest.py b/tests/harnesses/claude_native/forwarder/test_ae_prompt_suggest.py
index b6479f96dcd535ebbf4ebb68f2a26fad59a3d980..bd47e1c49ef674c78cb39fd8efc66d531136a35e 100644
--- a/tests/harnesses/claude_native/forwarder/test_ae_prompt_suggest.py
+++ b/tests/harnesses/claude_native/forwarder/test_ae_prompt_suggest.py
@@ -311,8 +311,14 @@ async def test_timeout_kills_the_whole_process_group(on_path: Path) -> None:
             os.kill(grandchild, 0)
         except ProcessLookupError:
             break
-        # A killed but unreaped child shows as a zombie; that is dead too.
-        if Path(f"/proc/{grandchild}/stat").read_text().split()[2] == "Z":
+        # A killed but unreaped child shows as a zombie; that is dead too. The
+        # reaper can remove it between the kill probe and this read, which also
+        # means dead.
+        try:
+            fields = Path(f"/proc/{grandchild}/stat").read_text().split()
+        except FileNotFoundError:
+            break
+        if fields[2] == "Z":
             break
         await asyncio.sleep(0.1)
     else:
